# Backend engineering — gestao_lancamento_de_chamados & aligned BFF repos

When implementing or reviewing **Python back-end** work for this product
(FastAPI BFF, Databricks App, Unity Catalog, ADO `access-requests-portal`, or
coordination docs), treat **`docs/BACKEND_ENGINEERING_CONTEXT.md`** (repository
root) as the **single source of truth** for architecture and quality bar.

## Binding rules (summary)

- **PEP 8** for all Python; clear public module docstrings.
- **SOLID:** thin HTTP layer; business logic not trapped in route handlers.
- **DDD:** separate **domain**, **application** (use cases), **infrastructure**
  (Databricks SDK, SQL); routes map HTTP ↔ DTOs ↔ use cases only.
- **TDD:** add or extend tests with every behavioral change when a harness
  exists; otherwise document manual checks and add the smallest locking test
  as soon as feasible.

## Default design stack (pluggable, FE-friendly)

1. **Hexagonal (ports & adapters)** — domain/application must not import
   `WorkspaceClient` or build raw SQL; use **ports** (`Protocol` / ABCs) and
   **adapters** in infrastructure.
2. **Repository** per aggregate (`Ticket`, events stream) with use-case-oriented
   method names aligned with future SPA `TicketsRepository` operations.
3. **Application services / one handler per use case** — new API behavior =
   new module + wire in router `deps`, not growth of monolith files.
4. **Pydantic at the boundary** + versioned **`/api/v1`** + **OpenAPI** as the
   shared contract with the front end (optional TS client generation later).

Identifiers, comments, commit messages, and technical Markdown stay **English**.
User-facing responses may follow product language when specified elsewhere.

## Git workflow per repository (binding)

This product is mirrored across two Git remotes with **different branching
contracts**. Always honor them.

### GitHub — `gregoryfiel/gestao_lancamento_de_chamados`

- **Agent backend docs (default for the backend agent):** always work on
  **`agent/backend-docs`**, reset to `origin/main` after each merged PR (same
  reset policy as the ADO agent branch).
- **Humans / release docs:** may still use **`v1.x.y`** branches as defined in
  [`.cursor/rules/frontend-agent.mdc`](./frontend-agent.mdc) §1 when preparing
  a versioned documentation drop.
- Conventional Commits in English. PR target: `main`.
- Never push directly to `main`.

### Azure DevOps — `data-platform-bees-consumer-mkt-strategy-insights`
(monorepo path `apps/access-requests-portal/`)

- **Agent backend (default for the backend agent):** always work on
  **`agent/access-requests-portal-backend`**, cut once from `master` and reset
  to `origin/master` after each merged PR (`git reset --hard` + push
  `--force-with-lease` on that branch only).
- **Humans / one-off tasks:** may still use `feat/access-requests-portal-…` or
  `fix/access-requests-portal-…` cut from `master` when they prefer isolated
  feature branches.
- Conventional Commits in English. PR target: `master`. Do not modify shared
  infrastructure files (`app.yaml`, `requirements.txt`, `.gitignore`,
  `workspace_auth.py`, `ticket_models.py`) unless the task explicitly requires
  it; CRLF/LF noise must not appear in commits.

### Cross-repo coordination

- Engineering doc canonical home: GitHub `docs/BACKEND_ENGINEERING_CONTEXT.md`.
  ADO carries only the pointer at
  `apps/access-requests-portal/docs/ENGINEERING_CONTEXT.md`.
- Never use destructive Git commands (force push, hard reset, branch delete on
  remote) on either remote without an explicit user request.

### Standing automation policy (no need to ask)

- **GitHub:** the agent MAY commit and push to **`agent/backend-docs`** (or a
  human `v1.x.y` branch when instructed) without asking. PR creation against
  `main` still requires explicit user intent unless previously scheduled.
- **ADO:** the agent MAY commit and push to **`agent/access-requests-portal-backend`**
  without asking, but **MUST NOT** create or update Pull Requests automatically.
- Both remotes: keep diffs minimal and commit messages Conventional + English.
